From f9c5be7c4cc8fb479fb3a21deb749247fc93f225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hizuru254 <2654837056@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:41:18 +0800
Subject: [06/14] tools: global-fit TBR estimator exposes a 2.6x method
 systematic

Adds tools/tbr_global_fit.py, which fits the whole temperature profile with a
piecewise-linear model (1 reference + 5 slopes + 4 interface jumps) instead of
fitting each 16 A window independently.

On run_v038 (flat, v1.6):
  window extrapolation (postprocess.py) : 5.33e-9 m2K/W
  global fit                            : 1.38e-8 m2K/W
The fit itself is sound (residual rms 1.1 K over 91 bins), so the discrepancy is
physical: the Au layer is NOT linear. Its gradient is -1.2 K/A within 8 A of
each interface and only -0.15 K/A in the middle 20 A, because Ti has dissolved
into the Au film and smeared the interface over ~10 A.

Shifting the assumed interface planes by +-3 A changes the global-fit total by
only +-7.6 % (1.384-1.489e-8), so the curvature inside the layers, not the plane
placement, is the dominant systematic.

Consequence: TBR_total of this stack is only defined to about a factor 2.6, far
above the 4-8 % statistical error reached by v1.6. Pattern differences below
~20 % cannot be resolved by running longer; the limitation is the model.
A 'method consistency' gate (window vs global fit within 20 %) is proposed but
NOT enabled, since changing QC criteria needs human approval.
